[32m+[m[32m# Vertex Velocity Web Panel 4.0.0 — build, push and release[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m> Do not publish a release until `mvn clean verify` succeeds and the shaded JAR starts on a test Velocity proxy. A Git tag does not prove the plugin is bug-free.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 1. Open the repository[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen the extracted project root in IntelliJ IDEA. The folder must contain `pom.xml`, `src/`, and `.github/`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. Confirm Java 25 and build[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIn the IntelliJ terminal:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mjava -version[m
[32m+[m[32mmvn -version[m
[32m+[m[32mmvn --batch-mode clean verify[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBoth Java and Maven must be available; Java must be version 25. The expected artifact is:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`target/vertex-velocity-web-panel-4.0.0.jar`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf the build fails, do not continue to tagging. Fix the first Maven error and rerun the command.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 3. Check Git status and commit[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRun these commands from the root of your existing Git clone (not a freshly extracted ZIP):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mgit status[m
[32m+[m[32mgit branch --show-current[m
[32m+[m[32mgit remote -v[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEnsure you are on the intended branch and `origin` points to `official-vertex-studio/velocity-web-panel`. Review the diff, then:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mgit add .[m
[32m+[m[32mgit commit -m "Release: Vertex Velocity Web Panel 4.0.0"[m
[32m+[m[32mgit push origin main[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf your default branch is not `main`, replace `main` with the actual branch name. If Git says there is nothing to commit, that is okay only if the intended 4.0.0 changes are already committed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4. Ensure the tag does not already exist[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mgit fetch --tags[m
[32m+[m[32mgit tag --list v4.0.0[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf `v4.0.0` is already listed, stop and inspect it; do not force-move a published tag. If no output appears, create and push the annotated tag:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mgit tag -a v4.0.0 -m "Vertex Velocity Web Panel 4.0.0"[m
[32m+[m[32mgit push origin v4.0.0[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 5. Watch GitHub Actions[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen the repository's **Actions** tab. The release workflow checks that the tag version matches `pom.xml`, runs `mvn clean verify`, checks for the expected JAR, and only then creates the GitHub Release. If the workflow fails, fix the cause and use a new patch version/tag (for example `v4.0.1`) rather than reusing or force-moving `v4.0.0`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 6. Test before replacing production[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInstall the resulting JAR on a test Velocity instance using Java 25. Check startup logs, open the configured HTTP panel address, test login and key pages/API endpoints, then check shutdown/restart. Back up the current plugin JAR and data directory before any production replacement.[m
